Notes on the async surface (why this phase grew)
------------------------------------------------
plink (console) drives WSAEventSelect + WSAEnumNetworkEvents over a
kernel32 event; PuTTY (GUI) drives WSAAsyncSelect with window-message
delivery.  NEITHER binary resolves select() except plink, and NEITHER
resolves the overlapped family (WSASend/WSARecv/WSAConnect/WSAGetOverlapped
Result) or the WSA*Event object calls (they build events with kernel32
CreateEvent).  ws2_32.c implements the observed async pair for real over a
zero-timeout select() readiness pump and keeps overlapped/IOCP a documented
named refusal — matching exactly what the binaries ask for, nothing more.
